<title>PHILIPPINES: Citra Philippine venture gets tax breaks.</title>
<headline>Citra Philippine venture gets tax breaks.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citra Metro Manila Tollways Corp, a joint venture between Indonesia's PT Citra and the state-owned Philippine National Construction Co was granted tax breaks for a highway project, officials said.</p>
<p>A Board of Investments official told reporters on Wednesday the company building a 30-billion peso elevated highway under a build-operate-transfer (BOT) project would be entitled to a three-year tax holiday as well as exemptions from customs duties on capital goods imports.</p>
<p>The Board of Investments grants tax concessions to projects it sees as beneficial to the country.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8934</p>
</text>
